course: dictionary
lesson: 15986
title: Usage: how words and things are used
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Usage is a word for the way something is used. It can mean how words are used in a language, what is right and normal, or how much of something is used. «In common usage, people say "bonkers" to mean crazy.» Here usage tells you what most people normally say.
explain: Usage can also mean an amount. «The app shows your data usage for each week.» Data usage is how much data your phone has used. Water usage and energy usage work the same way: they tell you how much water or energy has been used.
explain: Look at the words around usage to find its meaning. If the sentence is about words or speaking, usage means the normal way of using language. If it is about numbers, bills or meters, usage probably means an amount. Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Usage means the way something is used.
fact: In English, usage can mean the normal way words are used, including what is right and what is common.
fact: In maths and science, usage often means how much of something is used, such as water usage per day.
fact: «Usage» can also mean the way something is treated, as in «the guide explains the usage of each tool».
fact: Common phrases: in common usage, water usage, data usage, usage guide.
exercise: «The water usage goes up in summer when people water their gardens.» What does usage mean here? | *How much water is used | The name of the water company | The place where water is kept | The colour of the water
exercise: «In common usage, people say "bonkers" to mean crazy.» What does "in common usage" mean? | Only one person uses it, in one book | *The way most people normally use it | It is against the law to say it | It is a very old word from another country
exercise: «The app shows your data usage for each week.» What is data usage? | A phone case | The speed of your internet | *How much data you have used | The name of the app
test: «The guide explains the correct usage of each tool in the shed.» What does usage mean here? | *The right way to use each tool | The price of the tools | The number of tools in the shed | The size of the shed
test: «Energy usage fell after the family switched off the lights.» What does energy usage mean? | The cost of the lights | *How much energy was used | The colour of the lights | The type of energy in the lights
exam: «Her teacher said the usage in her story was not quite right, so she checked her verbs.» What does usage mean in this sentence? | The title of the story | The length of the story | How many stories she wrote | *The way words are used in the language
